{
  "date": "2026-10-18",
  "category": "finance",
  "title_zh": "美联储主席沃什：九月加息不是新一轮紧缩的开始",
  "title_en": "Fed Chair Warsh: September's rate hike is not the start of a new tightening cycle",
  "paragraphs": [
    {
      "zh": "10月17日，美联储进入“静默期”。在这之前，美联储主席沃什在曼谷参加国际货币基金组织年会时发言。他表示，9月的加息只是收回了一部分宽松政策，并不代表新一轮紧缩的开始。",
      "en": "On October 17, the Federal Reserve entered its \"quiet period.\" Before that, Fed Chair Kevin Warsh spoke at the IMF annual meetings in Bangkok. He said September's rate hike only withdrew part of the easy policy and does not mark the start of a new round of tightening."
    },
    {
      "zh": "沃什说，美联储会在10月和12月的会议上重新评估经济增长、就业和通胀情况，每次会议单独做决定。他还认为，从中期来看，人工智能会提高生产效率，对经济有好处；但是短期内，大量的AI投资可能会推高需求和物价。",
      "en": "Warsh said the Fed will reassess growth, jobs and inflation at its October and December meetings, deciding meeting by meeting. He also believes that over the medium term AI will raise productivity and be good for the economy, but in the short term heavy AI investment may push up demand and prices."
    },
    {
      "zh": "不过，美国的通胀压力仍然不小。9月美国消费者价格指数（CPI）同比上涨3.7%，高于市场预期。市场数据显示，投资者认为美联储10月再次加息的可能性一度上升到接近50%。",
      "en": "However, US inflation pressure is still significant. In September the US consumer price index (CPI) rose 3.7% year-on-year, above market expectations. Market data showed that the chance investors saw of another Fed hike in October at one point rose to nearly 50%."
    },
    {
      "zh": "下一次议息会议将在10月27日至28日举行，全球市场都在关注结果。",
      "en": "The next rate-setting meeting will be held October 27–28, and markets around the world are watching the outcome."
    }
  ],
